.TH AVR\-GROUP\-MEMBER\-LIST 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-member-list \- List a group's direct members.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group member list
[OPTIONS] GROUP
.SH DESCRIPTION
List a group's direct members.
.PP
GROUP is a group ID (grp-...), the group's path from the root group, such as Organization/Platform/CI, or the end of a path when only one group has it, such as Platform/CI.
.PP
Members of subgroups are listed with the subgroup.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr group member list Platform/CI
    avr group member list Platform/CI -L 1000 --json user_id,email
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    added_at, email, name, source, stale_sources, user_id
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIGROUP\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max members to return. (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-group-member (1),
.BR avr-group-member-add (1),
.BR avr-group-member-remove (1)
